Package: optLump
Title: Lumping Categorical Covariates in a Way that Preserves Information
Version: 0.0.1.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Daan Olivier", family = "Koning", email = "daanolivierkoning@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(given = "Martijn", family = "Ruppert", email = "m.ruppert@lapp.nl", role = "rev"),
    person(given = "Leiden Advanced Pharmacokinetics & Pharmacodynamics", role = c("cph", "fnd")),
    person(given = "Valentina", family = "Masarotto", email = "v.masarotto@math.leidenuniv.nl", role = "ths"),
    person(given = "Arno", family = "Knobbe", email = "a.j.knobbe@liacs.leidenuniv.nl", role = "ths"))
Description: Takes a categorical covariate and lumps (combines) multiple of the levels together. The way it chooses to do this is by optimizing for the preservation of mutual information between the pre- and post-lumping variables. Support exists for ordinal, hierarchical, and fully nominal variables.
